From fc079af33c0b3a52fdaf7e7751b3cfb175d42018 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dev <dev@example.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:34:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B3: role-scoping via capability-entry tags (eo/registry.py,
 eo/capabilities.py)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- backend/eo/registry.py: per-role metadata (the same store
  list_role_metadata()/get_role_metadata() already read/write) gets an
  additive `capability_tags: list[str]` field, defaulting to [].
  Wired into every place an entry gets constructed or migrated:
  _wrap_legacy_entry() (bare-string legacy entries), _load_prompts()'s
  migration pass (already-dict entries from before this patch),
  add_role_prompt() (preserved across a brief rewrite, same as
  pinned/times_hired), record_role_hire(), and set_role_pinned()
  (bare-entry fallback in both). New backend/eo/registry.py::
  set_role_capability_tags(role_name, tags, user_id=None) -> dict sets
  it explicitly -- replaces wholesale, same "explicit set, not an
  implicit accumulate" contract update_role_prompt() already uses for
  briefs, and creates a bare entry for a not-yet-hired role, same
  discipline as record_role_hire()/set_role_pinned().
- backend/eo/capabilities.py: new get_role_scope(role_name, user_id=None)
  -> list[str], a thin read of the field above (empty list for both
  "role has no tags" and "role doesn't exist" -- callers never need to
  tell those apart). New capabilities_for_role(role_name, user_id=None)
  -> list[dict], composing get_role_scope() with B1's list_capabilities()
  -- an untagged role sees nothing through this function (deliberately
  NOT "no tags means see everything").
- Test: backend/tests/unit/test_eo_role_scope.py -- capability_tags
  defaults/migrates/persists correctly across every registry.py write
  path above, get_role_scope()'s empty-list cases, and
  capabilities_for_role()'s tag-filtering (incl. union across multiple
  tags, empty for untagged/unknown roles, and confirming redaction
  entries never leak through even if tagged the same as a capability
  entry).
- Full backend unit suite re-run after this patch: 3449 passed, 7
  skipped, 2 xfailed, 0 failed (+16 over the B2 baseline, all new;
  nothing else changed).

Ref: MiniMe-CLI-Internal-Architecture-Plan.md §3.2 (role-scoping bullet), §7 (decided)
Ref: MiniMe-Patch-Series-B-Plan.md, Patch B3
Depends on: Patch B1 (list_capabilities()/entry_type mechanism must exist). Independent of Patch B2 (different files).
---
